<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>go-authn – Sdcreds</title><link>https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/tags/sdcreds/</link><description>Recent content in Sdcreds on go-authn</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/tags/sdcreds/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>sdcreds — systemd credentials, without systemd</title><link>https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/libraries/sdcreds/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://go-authn.github.io/docs/0.11/libraries/sdcreds/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What if a service needs the credentials a systemd unit gets from&lt;code&gt;LoadCredentialEncrypted=&lt;/code&gt;, and there is no systemd?&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;sdcreds&lt;/code&gt; reads and
writes the &lt;a href="https://systemd.io/CREDENTIALS/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;systemd credential&lt;/a&gt; format(&lt;code&gt;systemd-creds encrypt&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;decrypt&lt;/code&gt;) from Go, with a command line and a helper
that gives an s6-supervised service the same &lt;code&gt;$CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supported keys: &lt;strong&gt;null&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;host&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;/var/lib/systemd/credential.secret&lt;/code&gt;) and&lt;strong&gt;host-scoped&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;--uid&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;--user&lt;/code&gt;). TPM2 and public-key credentials are
recognised and refused with &lt;code&gt;*UnsupportedModeError&lt;/code&gt;; nothing is guessed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="install"&gt;Install&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="install"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#install" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
