&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="s6"&gt;s6&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="s6"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#s6" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;sdcreds s6-run --service&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;web --user&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;svc --source&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;/etc/creds -- /usr/bin/web&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;s6-run&lt;/code&gt; decrypts every file of &lt;code&gt;--source&lt;/code&gt; &lt;strong&gt;before&lt;/strong&gt; mounting anything, mounts
a per-service &lt;code&gt;tmpfs&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;nodev,noexec,nosuid,nosymfollow,noswap&lt;/code&gt;, mode 0700, size
and inode count bounded; &lt;code&gt;ramfs&lt;/code&gt; if the kernel lacks those options), writes the
plaintext 0400 owned by the service user, remounts it read-only, sets&lt;code&gt;CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY&lt;/code&gt;, then starts the service in a child that drops
privileges (&lt;code&gt;no_new_privs&lt;/code&gt;, an empty capability set) and waits for it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;s6-run&lt;/code&gt; is still the process that s6 supervises: it forwards &lt;code&gt;TERM&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;INT&lt;/code&gt;,&lt;code&gt;HUP&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;QUIT&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;USR1&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;USR2&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;ALRM&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;CONT&lt;/code&gt; to the service, exits with its
status (128 plus the signal number if a signal killed it), hands on the
descriptors it was given, and the service is killed if &lt;code&gt;s6-run&lt;/code&gt; dies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The credentials are taken away when the service ends, and before &lt;code&gt;s6-run&lt;/code&gt;
fails if the program cannot be executed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The mount lives in a private namespace by default (&lt;code&gt;--unshare=false&lt;/code&gt; turns
that off), so it disappears with the service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A credential sealed with the null key is refused unless &lt;code&gt;--allow-null&lt;/code&gt; is
given, and one that carries no name is always refused.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;sdcreds s6-finish --service=web&lt;/code&gt; unmounts lazily and removes the directory;it is idempotent. With &lt;code&gt;--unshare=false&lt;/code&gt;, a &lt;code&gt;SIGKILL&lt;/code&gt; of &lt;code&gt;s6-run&lt;/code&gt; leaves the
mount in place until &lt;code&gt;s6-finish&lt;/code&gt; runs: put it in the finish script of the
service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At most 1024 credentials and 16 MiB per service. Linux only; elsewhere the
commands report &lt;code&gt;ErrUnsupported&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The key files named by &lt;code&gt;--secret&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--machine-id-file&lt;/code&gt; must be root-owned and
not writable by group or others, and so must every directory above them up to&lt;code&gt;/&lt;/code&gt;. The key file is opened once, without following a final link, and the key
is wiped from the memory of &lt;code&gt;s6-run&lt;/code&gt; when it is done with the credentials. Only
the child takes the identity of the service; &lt;code&gt;s6-run&lt;/code&gt; and all its threads stay
root.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="interop"&gt;Interoperability&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="interop"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#interop" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Both directions are tested against the real &lt;code&gt;systemd-creds&lt;/code&gt; &lt;strong&gt;262.2&lt;/strong&gt;, built
from the &lt;code&gt;v262.2&lt;/code&gt; tag (no distribution package).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;testdata/systemd-v262.2&lt;/code&gt; holds 44 credentials written by systemd-creds (null,host and host-scoped; with and without a name; no, past and future not-after;0 B, 1 B and 64 KiB payloads; five tampered variants), and &lt;code&gt;manifest.json&lt;/code&gt;
records what systemd-creds itself answered for each of 272 decryption attempts(right and wrong name, before and after not-after, with and without &lt;code&gt;--uid&lt;/code&gt;).The library gives the same answer, with the same class of error, for every
one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;With a fixed IV, &lt;code&gt;Encrypt&lt;/code&gt; reproduces systemd&amp;rsquo;s bytes exactly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In the container, &lt;code&gt;systemd-creds decrypt&lt;/code&gt; opens what &lt;code&gt;Encrypt&lt;/code&gt; wrote, and the
command line passes the same round trip in both directions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-code-block hx:relative hx:mt-6 hx:first:mt-0 hx:group/code"&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-sh" data-lang="sh"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;docker build -t sdcreds-interop docker
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;docker run --rm --privileged -e &lt;span class="nv"&gt;SDCREDS_REQUIRE_SYSTEMD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; -e &lt;span class="nv"&gt;SDCREDS_S6_INTEGRATION&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="m"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="se"&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; -v &lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;$PWD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;:/src/sdcreds -w /src/sdcreds sdcreds-interop &lt;span class="se"&gt;\
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; sh -c &lt;span class="s1"&gt;&amp;#39;echo 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef &amp;gt; /etc/machine-id &amp;amp;&amp;amp; go test -count=1 ./...&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="hextra-code-copy-btn-container hx:opacity-0 hx:transition hx:group-hover/code:opacity-100 hx:flex hx:gap-1 hx:absolute hx:m-[11px] hx:right-0 hx:top-0"&gt;
&lt;button
class="hextra-code-copy-btn hx:group/copybtn hx:cursor-pointer hx:transition-all hx:active:opacity-50 hx:bg-primary-700/5 hx:border hx:border-black/5 hx:text-gray-600 hx:hover:text-gray-900 hx:rounded-md hx:p-1.5 hx:dark:bg-primary-300/10 hx:dark:border-white/10 hx:dark:text-gray-400 hx:dark:hover:text-gray-50"
title="Copy code"
aria-label="Copy code"
data-copied-label="Copied!"
&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-copy-icon hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:hidden hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="hextra-success-icon hx:hidden hx:group-[.copied]/copybtn:block hx:pointer-events-none hx:h-4 hx:w-4"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/button&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Without &lt;code&gt;SDCREDS_REQUIRE_SYSTEMD=1&lt;/code&gt; the tests that need the binary are skipped;CI sets it, so an absent binary is a failure there. The 1 MiB boundary is
covered by the library tests only, not by interop vectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="deviations"&gt;Deviations from systemd&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="deviations"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#deviations" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A host secret whose machine id does not match is &lt;strong&gt;refused&lt;/strong&gt;
(&lt;code&gt;ErrHostKeyMachine&lt;/code&gt;); systemd removes it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;--with-key=auto&lt;/code&gt; means &lt;code&gt;host&lt;/code&gt;: there is no TPM2 here.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A credential sealed with the null key has no secrecy: &lt;code&gt;sdcreds decrypt&lt;/code&gt;
refuses it on every machine unless &lt;code&gt;--allow-null&lt;/code&gt; is given (systemd instead
consults the TPM2 and SecureBoot state; that library policy,&lt;code&gt;SystemNullPolicy&lt;/code&gt;, is not used by the CLI).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;code&gt;SDCREDS_MACHINE_ID_FILE&lt;/code&gt; (&lt;code&gt;encrypt&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;decrypt&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;setup&lt;/code&gt;) points at another
machine id file. &lt;code&gt;s6-run&lt;/code&gt; ignores it and &lt;code&gt;SYSTEMD_CREDENTIAL_SECRET&lt;/code&gt;: its key
comes from the default files, or from &lt;code&gt;--secret&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;--machine-id-file&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A variable IV size is accepted when reading, as in systemd; this library
always writes 12 bytes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The secret is opened without following a final symlink, and must be a regular
file with one link and mode &lt;code&gt;0400&lt;/code&gt;, as systemd requires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="safety"&gt;Safety&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="safety"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#safety" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Every length is checked before it is used, before anything is allocated, and on
both sides of its bound; credentials are limited to 1 MiB (as systemd) and the
host secret to 16 MiB. The parsers are fuzzed in CI with the corpus committed,and &lt;code&gt;govulncheck&lt;/code&gt; runs in CI. The README has no performance table yet: the
measurement is deferred, an open item and not a result.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-hextra-search-id="reference"&gt;Reference&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="reference"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#reference" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The README at&lt;a href="https://github.com/go-authn/sdcreds" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;github.com/go-authn/sdcreds&lt;/a&gt; is the source
of truth for this page. See the module&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;LICENSE&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>